From 9beabed5286e5b5110042b8722b88f69be37e45b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:55:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 159/160] hydra: randomfloat and randomcolor from the library's
 nodegraphs

ND_randomfloat and ND_randomcolor were mapped to the white noise texture,
which has no `in`, `min`, `max` or `seed`: the delegate warned that the
input was dropped and the range ignored, and the value came from the
texture coordinate, in 0..1, the same for every seed. The mapping is
removed; the two expand from the library's own nodegraphs, a cellnoise2d
of `in` and `seed` ranged to min..max, as Karma evaluates them. The NEPAL
procedural materials, which draw per-instance randomness from them, now
match Karma within 1 % (K-116).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/material.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/hydra/material.cpp b/src/hydra/material.cpp
index 9f249c04..ca20f03f 100644
--- a/src/hydra/material.cpp
+++ b/src/hydra/material.cpp
@@ -2708,8 +2708,9 @@ const std::vector<MtlxEntry> &MtlxTable()
       {"ND_unifiednoise3d_float", &kMxUnified3dF},
       {"ND_unifiednoise3d", &kMxUnified3dC},
       {"ND_flake", &kVoronoi},
-      {"ND_randomcolor", &kWhiteNoise},
-      {"ND_randomfloat", &kWhiteNoise},
+      /* randomfloat and randomcolor expand from the library's nodegraphs
+       * (cellnoise2d of `in` and `seed`, ranged to min..max): mapped to a
+       * white noise they dropped `in`, `min`, `max` and `seed` (K-116). */
       {"ND_checkerboard", &MtlxCheckerboard},
       {"ND_clamp_", &kClamp},
       {"ND_remap_", &kRemap},
